chanprobe (0.4.2) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Make the 3600 Hz carrier mute (60 tones, 10 mute carriers). Crest
    factor 5.7 dB, L1 RMS level -5.7 dBFS (peak unchanged at -3 dBFS).
  * Results message version 5.

 -- Célestine GRAMAIZE <celestine+dev@gramaize.eu>  Mon, 16 Nov 2026 11:00:00 +0000

chanprobe (0.4.1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Probing pattern: 200 ms guard tone, 1 s L1, 200 ms guard tone, 1 s L2,
    200 ms guard tone. Each level is located from the end of the guard tone
    before it; no level ramp between L1 and L2.
  * The middle guard tone duration is reported along with the others.
  * A transmission that ends after the middle guard tone gives L1 results
    and reports L2 as not received.

 -- Célestine GRAMAIZE <celestine+dev@gramaize.eu>  Mon, 16 Nov 2026 10:00:00 +0000

chanprobe (0.4.0) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Two-level probe, as V.34 L1 / L2: the probe is sent at full level (L1),
    then 6.02 dB lower (L2), 1 s each (G L1 L2 G).
  * New level-dependence results: compression and AM/PM per carrier, overall
    level step, distortion in every mute carrier at both levels separated
    from the noise, and the order of that distortion.
  * Mute carriers now show the noise in their bin; distortion is reported
    separately.
  * Results message version 4 (508 bytes, one DATAC1 frame); SNR travels with
    0.5 dB resolution.
  * CSV output: new columns for compression, AM/PM, noise and distortion.
  * Fix the alignment of the table separators.

 -- Célestine GRAMAIZE <celestine+dev@gramaize.eu>  Mon, 16 Nov 2026 09:00:00 +0000

