chanprobe (0.3.1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Fix a crash when building the results burst with codec2 1.0.x (Debian
    bookworm): enabling the codec2 clipper also enables a transmit band-pass
    filter that codec2 1.0.x does not define for DATAC1, leaving it
    uninitialised. Neither is used any more; the peak level is limited by
    chanprobe (about -5.5 dBFS at -10 dBFS RMS).

 -- Célestine GRAMAIZE <celestine+dev@gramaize.eu>  Sun, 15 Nov 2026 19:00:00 +0000

chanprobe (0.3.0) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Results data link: replace Bell 202 AFSK by the codec2 FreeDV DATAC1
    OFDM data modem (LDPC FEC, pilot-aided equalisation). About 6 dB more
    margin on a 300-3000 Hz channel, and survives 80 ms dropouts.
    New build dependencies: libcodec2-dev, libsamplerate0-dev.
  * Probe analysis: audio continuity check (dropouts, sample slips), shown
    for both directions.
  * Results message version 3.

 -- Célestine GRAMAIZE <celestine+dev@gramaize.eu>  Sun, 15 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0000

chanprobe (0.2.2) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Results receiver: detect the start of a burst from its HDLC preamble
    flags and its end from the closing flags, instead of a level-independent
    signal-quality measure that also fires on voice-band receiver noise.
    A squelch-noise blip no longer ends the wait before the burst arrives,
    and open-squelch noise no longer keeps the receiver waiting.
  * Hard deadlines: no burst within --timeout, or a burst that has not
    completed within the longest possible frame time, ends the wait.
  * More precise clock offset estimate (long-baseline refinement).
  * Self test: voice-band channel with open squelch, squelch blips.

 -- Célestine GRAMAIZE <celestine+dev@gramaize.eu>  Sun, 15 Nov 2026 16:00:00 +0000

chanprobe (0.2.1) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Report the phase anomaly of each carrier (received minus sent phase,
    minus the best straight-line fit) instead of referencing it to the
    1050 Hz carrier. Amplitudes stay relative to 1050 Hz.

 -- Célestine GRAMAIZE <celestine+dev@gramaize.eu>  Sun, 15 Nov 2026 14:00:00 +0000

chanprobe (0.2.0) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Measure how long the guard tones and the results burst were heard, and
    hint at a clipped start or end of the remote transmission.
  * Report the received probe level (dBFS RMS) on both sides.
  * Results message version 2 (adds level and guard tone durations).
  * Lengthen the results burst postamble to 100 ms so that a clipped tail
    no longer destroys the frame.
  * Log PTT and audio timing of every transmission with -v; wait for the
    queued audio when a plugin returns from drain early.

 -- Célestine GRAMAIZE <celestine+dev@gramaize.eu>  Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000

